  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P><STRONG>Madonna's the new JK Rowling</STRONG>.&nbsp; <STRONG>Surprisingly, her books are just as popular with children, as the Harry Potter series</STRONG>.</P>
<P>2005-06-16 16:00 / moneycontrol.com</P>
<P><STRONG>She's the queen of Pop</STRONG> music and is <STRONG>still giving her much younger peers a run</STRONG> for their millions. She has always reinvented hersef at every stage in her life - from a rebel child to a vampy, platinum blonde image to all those shock tactics on stage with Prince and lately with Britney Spears - she's evolved into a yoga practicing and kabbalah believing, hip London mom. Now she's also written books for children. <STRONG>That's Madonna Louise Veronica Ciccone for you, better known as only Madonna.</STRONG> Not content with the music icon status, she's taken to literature in a big way. But if you're waiting for another book that will show you more of Madonna and her friends, you're in for a surprise. Her latest book is called <STRONG>'Lotsa de Casha'</STRONG> and since it's by the Material Girl, you may be forgiven for thinking this is another one of Madonna's 'kiss and tell' books. But you'd be surpised to know that this is her fifth book for kids and <STRONG>her previous books have been received with joy and glee by kids of all ages</STRONG>. And no, the books do not contain inappropriate references to adult activities. What's more, she has more things lined up. She's quite busy these days with a documentary that she's directed and a new album of dance music that she's putting together. All this, apart from taking the time out to be a mentor to Britney Spears. So <STRONG>if you're looking for a book, which you and your kids can curl up with this weekend, then try 'Lotsa De Casha'. </STRONG></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
