    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>Our friend <STRONG>George</STRONG> Kellis called &nbsp;<STRONG>Warner Vision In Australia</STRONG>&nbsp;and told them about our petition to bring the<STRONG> Virgin Tour</STRONG> and <STRONG>Blond Ambition on DVD</STRONG>. ..<EM>The man said, "What Madonna concerts did you say again?", I told him again and then he said "<STRONG>Those are going to be released on DVD</STRONG>," I asked when and he said "<STRONG>Not till early next year</STRONG>."</EM></P>
<P>In the meantime <STRONG>It appears that the Blond Ambition Tour has actually been released on DVD in Europe</STRONG>. Mainstream record stores in<STRONG> Germany </STRONG>are now stocking it and it is released in <STRONG>Holland on 20th June.</STRONG> <BR>It has <STRONG>nothing to do with Warners</STRONG> and has been issued by a legitimate company called <STRONG>FNM Falcon Neue Medien</STRONG> who specialise in old and re-issued films. It appears to be an <STRONG>authorised DVD</STRONG> although <STRONG>Drownedmadonna</STRONG>'s contacts are checking into this. </P>
<P align=center><IMG height=272 src="http://www.madonnavillage.it/drownedmadonna/badvd.jpg" width=600 border=0></P>
<P align=center><STRONG>BLOND AMBITION TOUR <BR>(HOUSTON; 05.05.1990) </STRONG></P>
<P align=center>Sound Format: Stereo <BR><EM>Regional Code: all <BR>Picture Format: NTSC 4:3 <BR>Running Time: 102 min. </EM></P>
<P align=center><EM>Producer: FNM Falcon Neue Medien </EM></P>
<P align=center><EM>EAN-Code: 4013659003366 </EM></P>
<P class=message-text-plain><EM>A&nbsp;very special thanks to <STRONG>Benjamin</STRONG> and <STRONG>George</STRONG></P></EM>
</font></div>
