    <td background="images/bg.gif"><font class=""><a href="modules.php?name=News&new_topic=8">Interviews</a></font><br><font class="testo_notizia" color="#000000"><b>[<a href="modules.php?name=&amp;file=categories&amp;op=newindex&amp;catid=2"><font class="esclusiva">EXCLUSIVE</font></a>] Drowned Madonna meets Alexandre Magno.</b></font></td>
  </tr>
  <tr height="1">
    <td  background="images/riga.gif"></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
	<div align=justify><font class="storytext"><P>We had the honour to interview <STRONG>Alex Magno</STRONG>, the choreographer of <STRONG>"The Girlie Show"</STRONG> and <STRONG>"The Drowned World Tour"</STRONG>. Since <STRONG>Alex</STRONG> has been very busy, it tooks over 8 months to arrange it, but it was worthy.&nbsp;</P>
<P><STRONG>Alex</STRONG> proved to be a great and complete <STRONG>ARTIST</STRONG>: dancer, choreographer, singer, actor and so on. And most of all he proved to be a unique human being.</P>
<P>Live <STRONG>"The Girlie Show"</STRONG> and <STRONG>"The Drowned World Tour"</STRONG> over again. Find out the creative process of two of the greatest and important <STRONG>Madonna</STRONG>'s tours. </P>
<P><STRONG>"In my opinion Madonna is who she is today thanks to her hard work and her many hours of dedication to perfect her craft, she is a complete perfectionist," said Alex.</STRONG></P>
<P>Click on the banner below to read this revealing interview.</P>
<P align=center><A href="http://www.drownedmadonna.com/modules.php?name=alex_magno" target=_blank><IMG src="http://www.madonnavillage.it/alex_magno/banner.jpg" border=0></A></P>
</font></div>
	</td>
  </tr>
